Once again Eidos delivers excellent stealth game, even though the plot is not as good as in Human Revolution, the gameplay of Mankind Divided is improved.

Amazing game so far, but it's plagued with problems.
Long loading screens;
flickering textures;
prompts that get stuck on the screen, even when you reload the game;
lack of vibration with the controller (even though the game supports vibration and it's in the option);
uneven performances.
Let's just hope the devs acknowledge the problems and fix them so I can recommend the game.
PS. even though the performances are uneven, they're not as bad as everyone are saying. The game is very much playable. It's not a bad optimized game per se, but it's not great either. There's still work to do in terms of optimization.
